WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.327
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.627 --> 00:00:09.164
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:14.590
Unit five: Possessives (my/your/his/her). Today you will show who owns something.

4
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.461
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.494
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.293
My.

7
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.877
My means belonging to me.

8
00:00:26.483 --> 00:00:27.763
This is my book.

9
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.817
Your turn. Say: My.

10
00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.482
My.

11
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:36.009
Your.

12
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:38.587
Your means belonging to you.

13
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.359
Is that your pen?

14
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.730
Your turn. Say: Your.

15
00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.452
Your.

16
00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:48.997
His.

17
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.600
His means belonging to him.

18
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:53.475
His name is Tom.

19
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:56.260
Your turn. Say: His.

20
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.020
His.

21
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:01.506
Her.

22
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:04.272
Her means belonging to her.

23
00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.210
Her name is Ana.

24
00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:09.005
Your turn. Say: Her.

25
00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:12.705
Her.

26
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.265
Our.

27
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.913
Our means belonging to us.

28
00:01:17.517 --> 00:01:18.889
Our teacher is kind.

29
00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:21.648
Your turn. Say: Our.

30
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.211
Our.

31
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.614
Their.

32
00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:29.233
Their means belonging to them.

33
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:31.329
Their classroom is big.

34
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.395
Your turn. Say: Their.

35
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:37.944
Their.

36
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:39.499
Belong.

37
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:42.599
Belong means to be owned by someone.

38
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:44.869
This bag belongs to me.

39
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:47.497
Your turn. Say: Belong.

40
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.230
Belong.

41
00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:52.764
Own.

42
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.179
Own means to have something that is yours.

43
00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.121
He owns a bike.

44
00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:01.253
Your turn. Say: Own.

45
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:04.857
Own.

46
00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:09.573
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:14.393
Visal, how do we say that a book is ours? Do we say 'I book'?

48
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:24.384
No. We use a possessive word: my book. I becomes my, you becomes your, he becomes his, she becomes her.

49
00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:27.367
What about more than one person?

50
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:37.559
We becomes our, and they becomes their. For example: our teacher, their classroom. The possessive word goes before the noun.

51
00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.671
Do these words change for singular and plural nouns?

52
00:02:42.783 --> 00:02:50.732
No. We say my book and my books, her pen and her pens. Only the owner changes, not the thing.

53
00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:53.286
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:59.865
Grammar focus: Possessives: my and your and his and her and our and their.

55
00:03:00.165 --> 00:03:01.386
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:03.293
my book (I own it)

57
00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.811
her name (it is a girl's name)

58
00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:08.577
their classroom (it belongs to them)

59
00:03:09.533 --> 00:03:15.216
My, your, his, her, our and their go before a noun and show the owner. They do not change for plural nouns.

60
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:19.264
Be careful! Don't say: She likes he book.

61
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.339
Say: She likes her book.

62
00:03:23.639 --> 00:03:25.905
Use her, not he, before a noun.

63
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.631
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:30.433 --> 00:03:31.423
Whose Is It?.

65
00:03:31.723 --> 00:03:34.047
This is my book, and that is your pen.

66
00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.323
His name is Tom, and her name is Ana.

67
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:39.822
Our teacher is kind.

68
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:43.959
Their classroom is big, and it belongs to the whole school.

69
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:47.187
Everyone must take care of what they own.

70
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.313
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.766
She likes blank new bag.

72
00:03:55.066 --> 00:03:57.837
A, his. B, her. C, my.

73
00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.016
The answer is B: her.

74
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.732
We love blank school.

75
00:04:06.032 --> 00:04:08.942
A, our. B, their. C, your.

76
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.697
The answer is A: our.

77
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.584
Tom has a bike. It is blank bike.

78
00:04:18.884 --> 00:04:21.771
A, her. B, his. C, my.

79
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:27.472
The answer is B: his.

80
00:04:28.617 --> 00:04:30.233
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:35.754
A, They are at their house.. B, They are at they house.. C, They are at them house..

82
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.915
The answer is A: They are at their house..

83
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.247
According to the reading, what is big?

84
00:04:45.547 --> 00:04:49.177
A, the pen. B, their classroom. C, my book.

85
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:55.267
The answer is B: their classroom.

86
00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:59.491
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.606
Whose book is it? Try answering with 'my' or 'his'.

88
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:13.940
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:27.312
It is my book. My name is on the first page. If the book belongs to my friend, I say it is his book or her book. We use my, his and her before a noun to show who owns it.

90
00:05:27.612 --> 00:05:29.252
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:36.192
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and possessives: my and your and his and her and our and their.

92
00:05:36.492 --> 00:05:39.818
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:05:40.118 --> 00:05:42.747
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

94
00:05:43.047 --> 00:05:45.293
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

